    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for vsftpd.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The vsftpd packages include a Very Secure File Transfer Protocol (FTP) daemon, which is used to serve files over a network.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* vsftpd: vsftpd: Denial of service via integer overflow in ls command parameter parsing (CVE-2025-14242)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
